%% Incident lane: Lambda timeouts at 2 a.m. (framework layer 3 example, layer 7 break-glass; Options §6).
%% E = incident responder, R = on-call approver (backup only if R is unavailable, OD2).
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor E as E (incident responder)
    participant AG as Agent sessions on E's laptop
    actor R as R (on-call approver)
    participant GH as GitHub (PR, ruleset)
    participant CI as Deploy job (OIDC role)
    participant AWS as AWS prod

    alt Main path: the pull request, with faster people, not fewer checks
    E->>AG: Analysis session, read-only roles: metrics, redacted logs
    AG-->>E: Proposes timeout, memory and queue visibility changes
    E->>AG: Edit session: change serverless.yml, diff on non-prod
    E->>GH: Open PR labelled incident, linked to the open incident issue (OD27), checks still run
    E->>R: Page (phone in phase 1, routed alert from phase 2)
    R->>GH: Review the diff, approve (R never writes the fix, OD7)
    E->>GH: Merge
    GH->>CI: Deploy: prod preview, risk stop, apply
    Note over E,CI: If the risk stop holds the deploy, its approval PR also gets the incident label and the same issue link, then R approves it
    CI->>AWS: Changes as the deploy role
    Note over E,AWS: Estimate 11 to 46 min against a 30-min target (to be measured first in rollout)

    else Fallback only when the PR path cannot be used (Actions down, broken pipeline, op not in IaC)
    E->>R: JIT request: command list, scope, reason, incident link (channel outside GitHub)
    R-->>E: Approve in Linear before the grant (R is not the requester)
    Note over E,R: JIT receiver checks signature, R not E, R on shift, incident open, allowed set, then grants (OD33)
    E->>AWS: InfraOperator-service, 1-h role session (window up to about 2 h), E types the commands, no agent in that terminal (D2)
    Note over AWS: After: CloudTrail writes compared with the command list (by hand in phase 1, a job from phase 2)
    E->>GH: Codify PR within the deadline, drift detection until it merges
    end
    Note over E,AWS: Approval before apply is met only partly here (accepted by the author, for Papaya Compliance sign-off)
